WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
Here's the build laid
onto Book 07's six waves.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.119
Wave one is a small test
cluster and read-only discovery,

3
00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:08.737
so you learn what you have.

4
00:00:08.737 --> 00:00:13.268
Wave two builds production properly
— two of everything, keys backed up,

5
00:00:13.268 --> 00:00:18.188
sign-in and logging done — and doesn't
close until a restore has been rehearsed.

6
00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:22.399
Wave three pilots automatic
renewal on a handful of servers,

7
00:00:22.399 --> 00:00:25.263
with the old method left
on as a safety net.

8
00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:29.102
Then you scale ring by ring,
move public certificates over,

9
00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:33.310
and finally retire CAs using the
platform's inventory as proof.
